"""EARS feature edit (Phase 2, Stage 3, criterion C6b + the ear line of the structure inventory + the P4 tip/lip cap).
Built from spec_ears.json and its one review check_ears.json (the fix list). Head-frame mm throughout
(partition.head_local(world) * 1000: x = the cat's LEFT, y = back, z = up); a field F is negative inside tissue.

WHAT IT BUILDS (per ear, L and R)
  Henry's pocket (cutaneous marginal pouch) as a REAL doubled skin flap with an open slot, replacing whatever the skin
  field has there (skin v1's Gaussian-smoothed, inset envelope fills Tripo's slot and keeps Tripo's fur wedge):
    * per section h (planes perpendicular to the ear axis, ears_base_<sd>.npz frame) the local coordinates are
      a = depth below the free edge along -m(h) (m = the measured mouth direction) and b = across the slot along n(h)
      (n = unit(A x m), signed toward the caudal-lateral side, where the flap is). E(h) = the measured free edge, D(h)
      = the measured slot depth below it, g50 / g90 = the measured wall gaps (spec tables pocket_sections_<sd>; L h
      -5.5..-2.75 from the B2 re-measure, the rest Phase 1 SOUND; all are Tripo-reference numbers, +-0.5 mm).
    * SLOT (air): a slab of width g(a) about a midline b_c(a) = -(g(a)/2 + t(a)/2) * (1 - a/D) - so the flap's
      mid-sheet passes through the measured free edge at a = 0 and the slot's floor centre lies on the measured
      floor point at a = D (check S3: ONE slot source, the parametric slot anchored on Tripo's measured edge, floor
      and gaps; Tripo's wall polylines are not used). Floor = a disk of radius g(D)/2 (a skin U-turn). Open 3 mm
      outward past the mouth. g(a) = g50 to a = D/2, lerp to g90 at 0.9 D, g90 below; never below G_MIN = 0.5 mm
      (check S2: resolution-aware minimum = 2 voxels of a 0.25 mm grid; Tripo's 0.2-0.48 mm minima are below its
      own 0.47 mm mesh edge, unresolved, not anatomy). The slot is carved with a HARD max (air by construction).
    * FLAP: a skin-only duplicature (anatomy.walls, imaios_cmp / lanz_wood_2005): a sheet of tissue thickness
      t(a) = T_EDGE (0.6) at the free edge -> T_ROOT (0.8) at the floor (anatomy.flap_thickness_tissue_mm 0.5-1.0,
      ESTIMATE, low confidence, flagged) whose inner face is the slot's lateral wall; its free edge is the sheet's
      rounded end (a U-turn of radius t/2 = the outer skin turning back into the inner skin). Check B2's fix: the
      flap tissue comes from anatomy, NOT from Tripo's lip (which grows ~1 mm per mm below the edge); the rest of
      Tripo's lip is OUTER-FACE COAT, allowed up to D_CAP = 4.0 mm (coat.json cheeks max, ESTIMATE: the photo shows
      the flap merging into the cheek fur). Where Tripo's wall lateral of the slot is thicker than flap + D_CAP the
      skin keeps the base field inset by D_CAP (the flap's root into the ear base / cheek), joined to the sheet by
      a smooth min of radius K_ROOT = 0.4 mm (spec S5) whose radius falls to 0 within 0.5 mm of the slot.
    * the base tissue lateral of the slot midline inside the pocket zone is REPLACED by the above (lerp weight over a
      0.5 mm band that lies inside the slot, where the hard carve wins anyway); medial of the slot the base field is
      kept and the carve makes the cartilage-backed medial (antitragic) wall.
  NOT built here (OPEN, see the result): the helix curl (S6/P5), the conch semitube + canal (S7/P6), the thin cupped
  shell (open decision D1, the person's call). Their inventory probes stay declared stubs (they FAIL).

THE COAT CAP (for the coat_field owner, applied at integration - this module does not change the coat field)
  coat_cap_mm(P_head_mm) -> the max PER-FACE coat depth (mm) the skin inset may use at P: at the ear tip it follows
  spec coat_depth_limits.tip.max_total_coat_depth_mm / 2 (both faces inset) from the envelope apex down to 4 mm,
  ramping (smoothstep) to no cap (inf) by 8 mm; on the pocket flap the edit replaces the field, so the cap there only
  keeps the free edge: outer-face depth <= FLAP_EDGE_CAP 0.4 mm within 1 mm of the free edge (inf beyond 3 mm).
  Use: d' = d - softplus-style smooth min(d, cap) -> skin_cap_apply(d, cap) below (smooth, k = 0.1 mm).

API
  REGION                  {"L": (lo, hi), "R": (lo, hi)} head-frame mm boxes the edit touches (outside: F unchanged)
  edit(P_head_mm, F_mm, D_mm=None) -> F_mm   vectorised; D_mm (the coat depth already in F at P, optional) makes the
                          root's extra inset exact (D_CAP - D_mm); without it the ear_back typical 0.9 mm is assumed.
  coat_cap_mm(P_head_mm) -> per-face cap (mm, inf where uncapped);  skin_cap_apply(d, cap) -> capped d
  PROBES                  {"henrys_pocket.L": f(Lmm, f, inp), ..., "ear_tip.L": ...} geometric probes on a mesh whose
                          vertices are head-frame mm (inventory_check --headframe gives exactly that)
Sources: spec_ears.json (tables, anatomy, coat_depth_limits), check_ears.json (B1, B2, S1-S3), ears_base_<sd>.npz,
coat.json (cheeks max 4.0, ear_back typical 0.9 - both ESTIMATE).
"""
